@startuml
title The Core Mental Model - One Bundle, Many Targets
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "Project folder = **Bundle**\n(databricks.yml + resources/ + src/)\n\nDescribes WHAT to deploy.\nNever mentions a specific\nenvironment in code." as bundle #E8F0FE

rectangle "Target: **dev**\ncatalog = proj_dev\nidentity = you\nmode = development\n(names prefixed, schedules paused)" as dev #E6F4EA
rectangle "Target: **staging**\ncatalog = proj_stg\nidentity = staging SP\nmode = production" as stg #FEF7E0
rectangle "Target: **prod**\ncatalog = proj_prod\nidentity = prod SP\nmode = production" as prd #FCE8E6

bundle --> dev : bundle deploy -t dev
bundle --> stg : bundle deploy -t staging
bundle --> prd : bundle deploy -t prod

note bottom of bundle
  A **target** answers WHERE and AS WHOM.
  The same unchanged source deploys everywhere;
  only ${var.catalog} and the identity differ.
  "Promoting to prod" = deploying the same
  bundle with a different -t flag.
end note
@enduml
